From c86afef27c8736f5bed0cf002042befb872e188e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <p@p>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:20:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Fix 36 defects found while porting this solution to Rust

19 files. Every change carries an inline comment saying what was wrong, so the
reasoning survives in the code rather than only in a commit message.

Applied only where the correct behaviour was unambiguous: crashes, silently
wrong values, and unchecked input. The 11 findings that would change observable
output in a way I could not verify from the source alone are documented in
FIXES-NOT-APPLIED.md with what each one needs in order to be decided.

Highlights:
  Colorf.operator== was infinite recursion; Equals always returned false
  Log.Assert had an empty body, masking failures in three other projects
  MDS track parsing was desynchronised by 80 bytes per block
  NRG v1 reversed a uint32 widened to long, seeking to ~2.3 exabytes
  Blob_CHD.Read never advanced byte_pos, corrupting multi-hunk reads
  glVertexAttribDivisor was never called, so instancing could not work
  ReadPixelInfo overran a 12-byte struct by 4 bytes on every pick
  OpenGL's terrain renderer was unreachable (7-element slot array)
