From 89e35d6b5aa59ccce49acfeee6a3b4ecdd740b77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <p@p>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:29:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Fix MurmurHash2's empty-input short circuit; record the
 NuGet assessment

The short circuit made the function unable to reproduce SMHasher's verification
value for any seed (reference MurmurHash2("", 256) is 0xD1E836D3; this returned
0). Every non-empty input already matched.

Safe to apply because the solution has exactly one MurmurHash call site -
ShaderLoader.CalculateShaderCacheHash - and its result keys an in-memory
Dictionary<uint, Shader> rebuilt every run, so no persisted value can be
invalidated. MurmurHash3 has no call sites at all.

Also assessed the NuGet options and recommend against a dependency: 66 verified
lines, one call site, and no package is both current and clearly maintained.
